/-
Johnson/G/SendsLit.lean: every sending of oracle messages in the seven plans of the verifier on
bytes, at the full-size and at the small example, as two written lists: what the verifier is told
at each.

`sendsOf` (Johnson/G/Sends.lean) is computed from public files by parsing, which Lean's kernel
does not evaluate. Here what it gives stands written out, for statements that the kernel is to
evaluate. Definitions only; the tests that hold the two lists against `sendsOf` are in
Johnson/G/SendsLitGuard.lean.

Main names:
  `SendLit`: a sending: which file's codes it stands under (0: the key file's; 1: the entry
    file's; 2: the proof file's); its chain's number in that file; the number of its entry "SEND
    seed" in the chain's plan, from 1; the oracle messages of the prover's message in the order of
    sending, each a shape with its class of leaves (`OnBytes.OracleNotice`), those without a
    sample among them.
  `sendsFullLit`: 119 sendings, 273 messages. `sendsSmallLit`: 46 sendings, 97 messages.

Whence the numbers: a program wrote the two lists from a print that Lean's evaluator made of
`sendsOf` at the three shipped public files policy.txt, layout.txt and KL.bin of
prover/examples/target_full_f2 (Johnson/G/KitFull.lean) and at the library's own copies of the
three shipped public files of prover/examples/target_small_f2_roomy
(OnBytes/Model/TestRecordWork.lean, OnBytes/Params/SmallFiles.lean). No other file was
read.

Limits: no theorem is stated. This file by itself holds the lists against nothing. Those of
Johnson/G/Sends.lean: which of the verifier's functions give a sending's list is that file's
reading of the verifier's text. A root that goes in an entry other than "SEND seed" (a fold's own
fresh mask) is in neither list.
-/
